      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T14:49:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does: `pkvm_make_req_to_host` is used when passing hypercalls to host for handling.\n\nThe `handle_vmcall,` is handled by `__vmx_handle_exit`/`vmx_handle_exit` which returns value is used by `__kvm_vcpu_enter_guest` where `handle_exit` is handled.\n\nBased on that (since during PKVM_GHC_SHARE_MEM handling in pKVM we return 0), `__kvm_vcpu_enter_guest` triggers\n`pkvm_make_req_to_host`:\n\n```\n          if (kvm_x86_call(handle_exit)(vcpu, exit_fastpath) \u003c\u003d 0) { \n                  pkvm_make_req_to_host(HOST_HANDLE_EXIT, vcpu);\n                  return false;\n          }   \n```\n\nright?\n\nMaybe:\n```\nThe motivation for it is the next patch in which pKVM requests memcache                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \nrefill from the host by forwarding the PKVM_GHC_SHARE_MEM hypercall to                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \nthe host (which happens via pkvm_make_req_to_host()) and there is a need                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \nto inform the host about refill size.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "6001d913_33a499e7",
      "revId": "3c0996b2c5fb9acac651f4e90633ec600de30f23",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
